    "problem_statement": "ChunkedReader.read_eof() returns None instead of raising RemoteProtocolError\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen a chunked transfer encoding connection is closed prematurely by the peer, the ChunkedReader should raise a RemoteProtocolError indicating an incomplete chunked read. However, it currently returns None instead of raising the expected exception.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport h11\nfrom h11 import Connection, SERVER, NEED_DATA\n\n# Create a server connection and start receiving a chunked request\nc = Connection(SERVER)\nc.receive_data(b'POST / HTTP/1.1\\r\\nHost: example.com\\r\\nTransfer-Encoding: chunked\\r\\n\\r\\n')\n\n# Get the request event\nrequest = c.next_event()\nassert c.next_event() is NEED_DATA\n\n# Receive partial chunk data\nc.receive_data(b'8\\r\\n012345')\ndata_event = c.next_event()\nprint(f\"Received data: {data_event.data}\")\n\n# Simulate connection close (empty bytes)\nc.receive_data(b'')\n\n# This should raise RemoteProtocolError but doesn't\ntry:\n    next_event = c.next_event()\n    print(f\"Unexpected: got {next_event} instead of exception\")\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f\"Expected exception: {e}\")\n```\n\nExpected behavior: Should raise `RemoteProtocolError` with message about incomplete chunked read.\nActual behavior: Returns None or some other value instead of raising the exception."
  }
